# What does NOT go into the distributed package.
#
# `git archive` (the zipball Composer builds `dist` from) honours `export-ignore`, so this
# list decides what lands in `vendor/aphexcoding/keyway-sso/` on a customer's server. It is
# kept in step with `archive.exclude` in composer.json, which is the `composer archive` path.
#
#  - `test/` and `bin/` are the test suite and its runner. They are part of this repository
#    on purpose - a plugin that guards sign-in should let you read what it is tested against -
#    but nothing on a production server has any use for them. `test/` also pins a throwaway
#    RSA key pair used to prove that a private key pasted into a certificate field is
#    REFUSED; it signs nothing and guards nothing, but on a customer's server it would set
#    off every SAST scanner as a leak it is not.
#  - `NOTES.md` is the maintainer's build log. It is not documentation and would only
#    mislead anyone reading it as such.
#  - `composer.lock` pins the versions this suite is run against. Composer ignores a
#    dependency's lock file, so nobody downstream reads it; the constraint that actually
#    applies is `require` in composer.json.
#
# `docs/` stays in the package deliberately: for an SSO plugin the deployment guides
# (Keycloak / Okta / Entra ID / troubleshooting) are part of the product, not a build
# artefact.

/test              export-ignore
/bin               export-ignore
/NOTES.md          export-ignore
/composer.lock     export-ignore
/.gitattributes    export-ignore
/.gitignore        export-ignore
